## Working model (Codex-specific)

- Prefer making the change, running the relevant checks, and reporting the result
  over stopping at a proposal. (Higher autonomy than the shared base implies.)

## What to suggest

- Catch correctness issues before style nits: error handling, race conditions,
  unbounded resource use, missing transaction boundaries, and missing tests for
  changed behavior.

## When working in this dotfiles repo

The repo at `~/Developer/personal/dotfiles` uses chezmoi conventions:

- Source files prefixed `dot_*` map to `~/.X`; `private_dot_*` adds mode 0600;
  `remove_*` markers delete the corresponding `~/.X`. Files ending in `.tmpl`
  are Go templates rendered with chezmoi data (name, email, signingKey, profile).
- The Brewfile is tiered: `Brewfile` (core, always) plus
  `brewfiles/Brewfile.{mac-apps,personal,work}`, layered by the brew-bundle
  script from the `profile` value and the `macApps` flag.
- Edit dotfiles via `chezmoi edit ~/.X` (editing the live `$HOME` file creates
  drift). Apply with the `chez` zsh function.
- `docs/mapping.md` is the authoritative source-to-target table — update it when
  adding/removing managed files.
